The new geometric theorem uses the actual full source. A normalized
stress whose positive diameter support is a star cannot use two
edges in a triangle-free source. The extreme leaf reactions force
straight unit contact chains along the two hull sides back to the
hub. Their first unit neighbors are at distance at most one:
strict inequality violates separation, equality makes a unit
triangle. A one-edge stress exists exactly for an actual integer
diameter with its complete straight unit chain, and is unique.

Hence if the preceding candidate's exceptional edge set E_0 lies
in one actual diameter star, its zero-reaction face P_0 is empty or
one exact chain stress. The star antecedent is not extracted from
a general source. In the singleton case, any internal chain point
r is actually unloaded and has positive contact reaction in that
stress. Intersect the source polytope with its zero-contact face;
this proper face has dimension at most s_Z-1 or is empty.
Helly then gives a stress-killing deletion of at most s_Z+1
labels, all in W except possibly r. The finite reduced-source
descent follows from Audit.87, retaining every contact isolate.
No extra deletion cost is added, but no label is restored.

