## Circumcircle half-depth closure and actual fan forests

The previous turn was progress: the sharp diameter-ball cap and the
source-realized forced-congestion family were committed at 4de98db4.
This run begins there, with fixed main 6e8dc144 and state Audit.155.
The chosen obligation remains a full-source finite move paying no
deletion: actual endpoint -> shallow lower-blocker-closed set ->
all-pair finite translation -> canonical lexicographic contradiction.
Every source label, including every contact isolate, is retained.

Read inputs: current STATE and C-II route, FS.1/FS.6 full-source
circumradius/midpoint geometry, C-I normalization, centered-fan
reflection/blocker injection and Audit.152's exact arrow closure.
The exact problem quantifiers and current route prompt were read.
No old report was used as an unqualified new premise.

The source circumball yields a sharper midpoint inequality. With
E=sqrt(R^2-D^2/4) and actual endpoint projection P, every increasing
crossing upper pair is strictly below D when the moving point has
depth < P-A, where A=E^2/delta+delta/2 for E<=delta/2 and
A=E+delta/4 otherwise. The two cases reduce to an exact quadratic
square identity or a monotone concave quadratic. The same complete
finite lower-closure argument now forces depth D/2-o(D) in the
canonical source, rather than (1-sqrt(3)/2)D. For R=D/2 the
finite threshold D/2-delta/2 is sharp; rational nonglobal sources
certify failure of a larger threshold. No finite correction is
claimed sharp for general R.

A new elementary source fact removes the old odd-cycle loss:
unique-partner degree-two fan leaves induce a forest of paths.
Their contacts are actual full-source hull sides, while a carrier
is a nonfan hull vertex of actual diameter degree at least three.
Thus an independent fan family has at least ceil(U/2) leaves.
Canonical blocker injection improves to ceil(U/2) disjoint
loaded-to-diameter-inactive first-blocker pairs. The subsequent
paths are not claimed disjoint, and no large U is extracted.

Actual KKT equilibrium at a unique-partner fan gives both incident
contact multipliers alpha=D^2 beta. Independent fan families
satisfy sum beta<=1/2; each full fan path with r roots pays
(r+1) beta_r from the normalized contact trace. These are weighted
budgets. No canonical multiplier floor, integer path-population
payment, shallow closure or Level I conclusion follows.

The first checker run caught a coefficient error in an auxiliary
factored identity: F(t)-D^2 factors as
(t-delta/2)(4E-3delta/2-t), not with coefficient -delta.
The analytic monotonicity proof had the correct derivative.
The certificate was corrected and its full final run passed.

Final exact checks: 966 quadratic identities; 261,916 valid
circumcircle cross pairs with 102,148 increasing pairs strictly
below D; nine finite sharpness fixtures and six arc fixtures
with 466 complete source pairs and 466 complete square-competitor
